# Trivy suppressions for the image scans in .github/workflows/docker-publish.yml.
#
# All three scans are blocking: a fixable HIGH/CRITICAL stops the publish before the image
# reaches GHCR. This file is the escape hatch when a release cannot wait for an upstream
# base-image rebuild - use it instead of re-adding `continue-on-error`, which silences every
# finding forever rather than one finding until a date.
#
# Format: one CVE per line, each with an expiry and a reason.
#
#   CVE-2026-12345 exp:2026-09-30  # <image>: <why we accept it> - tracked in #<issue>
#
# Rules:
# - Always set `exp:`. An entry without one never comes back for review.
# - Keep the window short (a few weeks). The expiry is a promise to revisit, not a deletion.
# - Say which image and why. "Not reachable from our code" is a claim someone must be able
#   to re-check when the entry expires.
#
# Unfixed CVEs do not belong here: `ignore-unfixed: true` already excludes them.

# Aucune exclusion en cours.
#
# 2026-10-08 : les sept entrees api-web (kin-openapi, grpc, x/crypto/ssh, suivies en #518 et #585)
# sont retirees. Elles venaient des modules Go compiles dans le binaire FrankenPHP 1.12.7 ;
# FrankenPHP 1.13.0 (2026-10-04) les met a jour, et un scan Trivy de
# `dunglas/frankenphp:1.13.0-php8-alpine` (HIGH/CRITICAL, corrigeables) ne trouve plus rien, ni dans
# le binaire ni dans Alpine, alors que le meme scan de la 1.12.7 trouvait exactement ces sept-la.
#
# 2026-10-10 : FrankenPHP 1.13.0 se fait rattraper par CVE-2026-78669 (golang.org/x/net 0.59.0, HIGH)
# et des CVE de la stdlib Go 1.27.1 compilees dans le binaire ; la publication api-web echouait sur
# develop depuis la #804. Passage a FrankenPHP 1.13.1 (2026-10-10) : le meme scan Trivy de
# `dunglas/frankenphp:1.13.1-php8-alpine` ne trouve plus rien, toujours sans exclusion.
